.TH KNOBU 1 "November 2026" "knobu 0.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
knobu \- PowerToys-style utilities for Ubuntu
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B knobu
[\fICOMMAND\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Knobu adds small power tools to the desktop: touchpad gestures for volume and
media, key and shortcut remapping, keeping the computer awake, a colour picker
and a text extractor. Without a command, it opens the settings app.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B settings
Open the settings app (the default).
.TP
.B enable
Start the background service now and at every login.
.TP
.B disable
Stop the background service and remove it from login.
.TP
.B status
Show whether the background service is running.
.TP
.BR awake " on|off|DURATION"
Keep the computer awake until turned off, or for a duration such as 30m or 1h30m.
.TP
.B pick-color
Pick a colour from the screen.
.TP
.B extract-text
Select an area of the screen and copy its text.
.TP
.B daemon
Run the background service in the foreground, for debugging.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/knobu/config.toml
Settings.
.SH NOTES
Reading touchpads and keyboards requires membership of the \fBinput\fR group.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/Aries-Surya/knobu
